==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|Mogor||obsolete}}
* {{alter|en|Mogul}}
* {{alter|en|Mughal}}

===Etymology===
Ultimately from {{der|en|ur|مغل|tr=muġal}}, variant of {{m|ur|مغل|tr=muġul}}, from {{der|en|fa|مغول|tr=muġul}}, from {{der|en|xng|ᠮᠣᠩᠭᠣᠯ}}. In early use via various European languages.{{attention|ur}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A head of the Mongolian [[dynasty]] founded by Zahīr-ud-Dīn Muhammed Bābur (1483-1530) which controlled large parts of southern Asia from the 16th to the 19th centuries.
# {{lb|en|now|_|historical}} A [[Mongol]] or [[Mongolian]], especially a member or follower of the Moghul dynasty.
# An [[important]] or [[successful]] person; a [[magnate]]. (Now usually as {{m|en|mogul}}.)

